1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,640
Hey, that's your target right over there.

2
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:12,760
The Tycoon, Mr. Batera.

3
00:00:14,040 --> 00:00:15,320
What am I watching?

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:18,160
Well, the Greed Island video game, of course.

5
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:21,120
But what makes you so interested in a video game, sir?

6
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:24,100
You've spent a considerable amount of money on it already.

7
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:27,360
The answer, my dear, is love.

8
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:31,280
When you fall in love with something, you want it all to yourself.

9
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:38,020
Love? Really? There are so many rumors flying around. Would you like to make a comment?

10
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:42,200
I'm gonna get my hands on the clue, Jean left.

11
00:00:57,360 --> 00:01:01,160
どうもいい?

12
00:01:01,160 --> 00:01:03,620
Am I right?

13
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:05,500
どうもいい?

14
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:35,480
You can fly away

15
00:01:35,500 --> 00:02:05,480
You can fly away

16
00:02:05,500 --> 00:02:35,480
You can fly away

17
00:02:35,480 --> 00:02:38,540
So I slept for half a day

18
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:41,980
Well, more like two days, buddy

19
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:45,800
Where's the boss? And what about the auction?

20
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:48,660
Oh, uh, they cancelled it completely

21
00:02:48,660 --> 00:02:52,440
The rest of the merchandise will be sold online

22
00:02:52,440 --> 00:02:55,080
The boss accepted that

23
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:58,120
Don't lie to me

24
00:02:58,120 --> 00:03:03,920
The boss was really looking forward to taking part in the auction

25
00:03:03,920 --> 00:03:06,880
I don't see her accepting that so easily

26
00:03:06,880 --> 00:03:11,660
The troop murdered Skuala

27
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:14,200
And Elisa

28
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:17,100
Well, she was inconsolable

29
00:03:17,100 --> 00:03:20,020
The Scarlet Eyes we won were stolen

30
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:21,400
But apparently

31
00:03:21,400 --> 00:03:26,560
The boss was more upset over Elisa's state than the loss of her prized possession

32
00:03:26,560 --> 00:03:31,840
That was when she informed us she wanted to go home

33
00:03:31,840 --> 00:03:34,380
I understand

34
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:37,040
Kouan and Killua

35
00:03:37,040 --> 00:03:38,980
They're both just fine

36
00:03:38,980 --> 00:03:40,280
And right now?

37
00:03:40,580 --> 00:03:41,220
He's out

38
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:48,000
Rest up

39
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:50,020
Your friends are doing what they have to

40
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:52,840
So you don't have to worry about a thing, okay?

41
00:03:52,840 --> 00:03:58,960
Our next item is the fabled game

42
00:03:58,960 --> 00:04:01,580
Known as Greed Island

43
00:04:01,580 --> 00:04:11,360
And it has a mysterious power

44
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,840
Let's take a look

45
00:04:12,840 --> 00:04:29,020
Now as I'm sure all of you can plainly see

46
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:32,800
A mysterious power protects the console from any damage

47
00:04:32,800 --> 00:04:36,940
Well, as long as someone is playing inside the game, that is

48
00:04:36,940 --> 00:04:40,420
This man is Jade Sari

49
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:43,840
He's the player who's inside the game even as we speak

50
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:46,460
As a matter of fact

51
00:04:46,460 --> 00:04:49,980
He's the one who signed a contract allowing us to auction it off

52
00:04:49,980 --> 00:04:53,840
So Jean didn't bring this one here

53
00:04:53,840 --> 00:04:58,800
Jade Sari left behind the following contract that stipulates

54
00:04:58,800 --> 00:05:02,800
If no one has cleared the game by the contract date

55
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:07,500
Even if he and the seven other players are still inside the game

56
00:05:07,500 --> 00:05:10,700
He would consign all seven units of the game

57
00:05:10,700 --> 00:05:12,200
As well as the consoles

58
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:14,200
To the Southern Peace Auction

59
00:05:14,200 --> 00:05:19,160
And entrust his dream of clearing the game to other challengers

60
00:05:19,160 --> 00:05:25,440
Unfortunately, when we received these units

61
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:27,600
The game had ended for two players

62
00:05:27,600 --> 00:05:31,980
Losing the game results in actual death for a player

63
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:35,880
This dangerous game requires that you risk your own life

64
00:05:35,880 --> 00:05:39,480
Only bid if you're prepared for the consequences

65
00:05:39,480 --> 00:05:43,780
The starting bid is 900 million, Jenny!

66
00:05:47,280 --> 00:05:48,600
I have 1 billion!

67
00:05:48,900 --> 00:05:49,880
1.5!

68
00:05:50,120 --> 00:05:51,880
Number 105 doubles it!

69
00:05:52,140 --> 00:05:54,360
71 doubles again to 6 billion!

70
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:55,940
Crap!

71
00:05:56,180 --> 00:05:57,140
My big brother!

72
00:05:57,140 --> 00:06:01,220
So you use your hand to tell her how much you want to bid?

73
00:06:01,900 --> 00:06:04,640
Yeah, the auctioneer looks at the crowd's hand signals

74
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:06,720
To discern the highest bid instantly

75
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:10,460
Number 16 doubles it again to 12 billion!

76
00:06:10,900 --> 00:06:11,940
What's this mean?

77
00:06:12,300 --> 00:06:15,240
201 doubles it again to 24 billion!

78
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:16,640
You idiot!

79
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:21,200
Number 16 bids 25 billion!

80
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,900
That was a close one

81
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:28,440
Okay, so I'm guessing he wasn't able to decipher that memory card

82
00:06:28,440 --> 00:06:32,640
I have 25.5 billion!

83
00:06:32,980 --> 00:06:34,640
How much money does he have?

84
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:39,460
Number 16 raises to 30.5 billion!

85
00:06:42,660 --> 00:06:49,800
30 and a half, is that right?

86
00:06:49,800 --> 00:06:52,680
It's of no consequence

87
00:06:52,680 --> 00:06:56,640
Or at least it won't be as long as we're able to clear the game

88
00:06:56,640 --> 00:07:01,280
Excuse us, but the two of us are hunters

89
00:07:01,280 --> 00:07:04,500
We're willing to offer our help in clearing Greed Island

90
00:07:04,500 --> 00:07:06,600
That's real funny

91
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:08,160
Now why don't you two run along?

92
00:07:08,240 --> 00:07:09,140
We're not joking!

93
00:07:09,360 --> 00:07:11,040
I really am a professional hunter!

94
00:07:11,260 --> 00:07:12,260
Sure you are

95
00:07:12,260 --> 00:07:14,880
I assume you have a hunter's license

96
00:07:14,880 --> 00:07:16,020
Yes, sir!

97
00:07:16,260 --> 00:07:18,140
It's at the pawn shop, remember?

98
00:07:18,140 --> 00:07:20,700
I don't have it on me

99
00:07:20,700 --> 00:07:22,540
What a surprise!

100
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:23,740
I knew he was lying!

101
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:24,620
No, I'm not!

102
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:26,860
Just hold on a moment

103
00:07:26,860 --> 00:07:29,880
The fact you're here at the auction in the first place

104
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:31,780
Tells me you're no ordinary children

105
00:07:31,780 --> 00:07:36,000
However, I can't take your word at face value

106
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:39,320
I am looking to hire professional hunters

107
00:07:39,320 --> 00:07:41,700
In order to clear this game, that much is true

108
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:45,340
But I'm afraid I simply can't hire either of you at this time

109
00:07:45,340 --> 00:07:48,600
Because there's a limit to the number of players you see

110
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:50,200
Not good

111
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,860
Did we fail already?

112
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:55,940
I'm thinking we don't actually need to buy the game

113
00:07:55,940 --> 00:07:58,440
Not if we just want the data inside it

114
00:07:58,440 --> 00:08:02,540
And I bet there are probably going to be some people who win Great Island

115
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:05,340
Who are going to look for other people to play it for them

116
00:08:05,340 --> 00:08:09,880
The number of players is limited?

117
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:15,080
Each memory card only has the capacity to store one player's data

118
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:20,340
With multi-taps, you can have a maximum of 8 players per console

119
00:08:20,340 --> 00:08:21,980
Hey, he's right!

120
00:08:22,560 --> 00:08:22,920
Remember?

121
00:08:23,300 --> 00:08:26,660
That Great Island save used up all 30 blocks on that memory card

122
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:27,980
Yeah

123
00:08:27,980 --> 00:08:29,580
How did you know?

124
00:08:30,080 --> 00:08:32,600
We got a Great Island save file a little while back

125
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,660
So we figured it out

126
00:08:33,660 --> 00:08:35,600
What about the game itself?

127
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,520
Have you played it?

128
00:08:37,080 --> 00:08:37,460
No

129
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:39,160
We only have a memory card

130
00:08:39,160 --> 00:08:40,260
Wait

131
00:08:40,260 --> 00:08:42,260
Does that mean...

132
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:45,180
If the memory card you speak of is real

133
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:47,180
You would still need another item

134
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:49,240
In order to remove the card from the console

135
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,520
You think maybe...

136
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:53,720
He means the ring

137
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:56,360
They know about the ring, too?

138
00:08:58,040 --> 00:09:02,100
It appears that these two boys may be worthy of our consideration

139
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,420
I assume you know Nen

140
00:09:04,420 --> 00:09:06,920
Let's have a demonstration of your Ren

141
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:08,780
Okay

142
00:09:08,780 --> 00:09:20,420
What do you think?

143
00:09:21,100 --> 00:09:22,240
Hopeless, I'm afraid

144
00:09:22,240 --> 00:09:24,440
Hiring them would be a complete waste

145
00:09:24,440 --> 00:09:28,220
They would simply run around in circles until they died

146
00:09:28,220 --> 00:09:31,880
How do you know when we haven't even tried?

147
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:34,560
It'd be too late by then, you see

148
00:09:34,560 --> 00:09:37,360
Better to die quick than squeak by

149
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:40,040
You would only be delaying the inevitable

150
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:44,180
See, as long as a player is alive inside the game

151
00:09:44,180 --> 00:09:45,520
You can't reset

152
00:09:45,520 --> 00:09:47,880
Nor can you remove the memory card

153
00:09:47,880 --> 00:09:51,460
In other words, it's impossible to send in new players

154
00:09:51,460 --> 00:09:56,880
I've personally hired around a hundred professional and amateur hunters to play this game

155
00:09:56,880 --> 00:10:00,020
And just over half of them have already given up

156
00:10:00,020 --> 00:10:01,360
What do you mean?

157
00:10:01,900 --> 00:10:04,860
They've given up on ever returning to the real world

158
00:10:04,860 --> 00:10:08,240
Choosing instead to live their lives inside the game

159
00:10:08,240 --> 00:10:11,720
That's why I'm so careful selecting players

160
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:15,580
We need people strong enough to obtain items

161
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:18,280
And then return them safely to the real world

162
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:20,680
So of course we have to be much more selective

163
00:10:20,680 --> 00:10:23,320
Are you trying to imply that we're not strong enough?

164
00:10:23,400 --> 00:10:23,660
Yeah

165
00:10:23,660 --> 00:10:25,660
Why does that guy think we can't do it?

166
00:10:26,360 --> 00:10:28,360
Because he is a professional hunter

167
00:10:28,360 --> 00:10:31,140
And one who has played Greed Island before

168
00:10:31,140 --> 00:10:35,640
Speaking from my own ample experience

169
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:39,320
The items we wish to bring here are easy to obtain

170
00:10:39,320 --> 00:10:41,680
With your paltry nen, it's hopeless

171
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:45,860
As a matter of fact, it'd be game over for you in no time

172
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:50,200
Once the screening is complete, I'll be returning to the game

173
00:10:50,200 --> 00:10:53,260
Wait, you're gonna be screening players while you're here?

174
00:10:53,660 --> 00:10:54,680
That's right

175
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:57,080
Starting on the final day of the auction

176
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:59,320
So if you're planning to participate

177
00:10:59,320 --> 00:11:02,960
I would recommend putting some additional work into your nen

178
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:04,960
We were gonna do that anyway

179
00:11:04,960 --> 00:11:06,500
Come on, let's go

180
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:08,320
Before you leave

181
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:10,840
How did you come to have a memory card?

182
00:11:12,240 --> 00:11:13,520
I'm not telling

183
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:17,720
Damn it

184
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,320
Those jerks

185
00:11:19,320 --> 00:11:22,280
We've definitely got to pass their screening now

186
00:11:22,280 --> 00:11:25,860
Screening, huh?

187
00:11:26,100 --> 00:11:27,100
So what's the plan?

188
00:11:27,520 --> 00:11:29,180
Do you even need to ask?

189
00:11:37,560 --> 00:11:39,200
We are bandits

190
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:41,100
We steal, of course

191
00:11:41,100 --> 00:11:45,140
Well, let's go back to the hideout and play it

192
00:11:45,140 --> 00:11:58,860
A memory card is already inserted

193
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:01,700
Which means only one more person can play

194
00:12:01,700 --> 00:12:04,280
We'll use a multi-tap

195
00:12:04,280 --> 00:12:06,180
Four more can play now

196
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:08,120
Very nice

197
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:10,320
So, who's gonna go in first?

198
00:12:10,320 --> 00:12:11,500
I will

199
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:20,080
He's really gone

200
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:22,780
I didn't think that would actually happen

201
00:12:22,780 --> 00:12:24,120
What was that?

202
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:26,280
It's a game

203
00:12:26,280 --> 00:12:27,520
You guys wanna play?

204
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:29,200
I pass

205
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,740
Maybe a little later

206
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:31,780
Fine

207
00:12:31,780 --> 00:12:33,320
I'll catch you later then

208
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:37,680
He disappeared too

209
00:12:37,680 --> 00:12:38,800
It's a game, right?

210
00:12:39,020 --> 00:12:39,620
What kind?

211
00:12:40,300 --> 00:12:41,640
It says right here

212
00:12:41,640 --> 00:12:43,660
That it's one where you can actually die

213
00:12:43,660 --> 00:12:46,540
It's listed in the catalog for the auction

214
00:12:46,540 --> 00:12:48,600
Hmm

215
00:12:48,600 --> 00:12:53,420
I can't believe he treated us

216
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:54,400
Like we're just dirt

217
00:12:54,400 --> 00:12:56,080
Damn it

218
00:12:56,080 --> 00:12:58,000
I know

219
00:12:58,000 --> 00:13:00,100
But you've gotta admit that he's got a point

220
00:13:00,100 --> 00:13:01,820
What do you mean?

221
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:03,740
Just chill out a little

222
00:13:03,740 --> 00:13:04,380
Look

223
00:13:04,380 --> 00:13:07,400
We should start thinking about taking all this to the next level

224
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:09,440
What are you talking about?

225
00:13:10,020 --> 00:13:10,420
Hatsu

226
00:13:10,420 --> 00:13:12,960
I mean our special attacks

227
00:13:12,960 --> 00:13:13,940
Huh?

228
00:13:14,620 --> 00:13:15,780
Think about it

229
00:13:15,780 --> 00:13:18,600
Kurapika started learning Nen the same time we did

230
00:13:18,600 --> 00:13:20,440
But because of his special attack

231
00:13:20,440 --> 00:13:22,780
He was able to take on the Phantom Troop

232
00:13:22,780 --> 00:13:25,940
Yeah

233
00:13:25,940 --> 00:13:27,880
With the powers that he obtained

234
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:30,460
He basically became invincible against them

235
00:13:30,460 --> 00:13:32,080
By placing his life on the line

236
00:13:32,080 --> 00:13:35,220
We can't limit ourselves

237
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:39,340
We need special attacks that fit our specialties

238
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:41,300
And that can minimize the risk

239
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,480
Something practical and effective

240
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:45,780
That's what we need to come up with

241
00:13:45,780 --> 00:13:53,140
I figured this would happen

242
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:55,700
Let's take one step at a time

243
00:13:55,700 --> 00:13:58,420
First off, what kind of abilities do you want to have?

244
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:00,360
That's a good question

245
00:14:00,360 --> 00:14:01,120
Well

246
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,940
Hey

247
00:14:03,940 --> 00:14:06,720
You must have an idea at least, don't you?

248
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:09,320
A really strong one

249
00:14:09,320 --> 00:14:11,100
Be more specific, man

250
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,440
To start with

251
00:14:12,440 --> 00:14:14,760
Think about something that's in your own category

252
00:14:14,760 --> 00:14:16,980
You're an enhancer, right?

253
00:14:17,420 --> 00:14:19,820
Try to think of a power that enhances something

254
00:14:19,820 --> 00:14:20,680
Okay

255
00:14:20,680 --> 00:14:22,120
Then think about

256
00:14:22,120 --> 00:14:23,780
What part you want to strengthen

257
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:25,580
And exactly how you want to do it

258
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:28,720
Hey, that hurt!

259
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:30,520
What ability do you want then?

260
00:14:31,080 --> 00:14:32,140
I already know

261
00:14:32,140 --> 00:14:35,920
And that's why I'm trying to help you out right now

262
00:14:35,920 --> 00:14:36,840
Really?

263
00:14:37,340 --> 00:14:38,120
What is it?

264
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:39,280
It's a secret

265
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:41,600
Gon

266
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,480
I'm gonna go practice my special attack now

267
00:14:44,480 --> 00:14:46,980
And you keep thinking about yours, okay?

268
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:48,540
If you don't

269
00:14:48,540 --> 00:14:50,900
I might be the only one who passes the screening

270
00:14:50,900 --> 00:14:56,540
If I don't put a little fear in him

271
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,860
Chances are he's only gonna get distracted

272
00:14:58,860 --> 00:15:04,420
Visualize my aura

273
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:06,640
Infused with electricity

274
00:15:06,640 --> 00:15:19,820
Then visualize discharging the stored electricity

275
00:15:19,820 --> 00:15:22,100
While refining my Nen

276
00:15:22,100 --> 00:15:30,660
With your paltry Nen

277
00:15:30,660 --> 00:15:33,260
It'd be game over for you in no time

278
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:35,520
Damn that guy!

279
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,360
I'll show him game over!

280
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,520
I see you're hard at work

281
00:15:39,520 --> 00:15:40,840
Kurabika!

282
00:15:41,220 --> 00:15:42,020
Feeling any better?

283
00:15:42,520 --> 00:15:42,880
Yeah

284
00:15:42,880 --> 00:15:43,980
My fever broke

285
00:15:43,980 --> 00:15:44,320
So

286
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,940
I'm alright now

287
00:15:45,940 --> 00:15:47,260
Wow

288
00:15:47,260 --> 00:15:49,440
He sure doesn't look alright

289
00:15:49,440 --> 00:15:50,420
But

290
00:15:50,420 --> 00:15:54,180
If Kurabika finds out that the spiders are still in York New City

291
00:15:54,180 --> 00:15:56,720
Will there be any way to stop him?

292
00:15:58,580 --> 00:15:59,320
Tell me

293
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:01,000
How did everything go at the auction?

294
00:16:01,460 --> 00:16:03,880
I believe you were going after an expensive game?

295
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:05,040
Uh

296
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:05,740
Yeah

297
00:16:05,740 --> 00:16:09,200
I see

298
00:16:09,200 --> 00:16:11,640
So they're screening players, are they?

299
00:16:12,520 --> 00:16:12,920
Hey

300
00:16:12,920 --> 00:16:15,480
What kind of training did you do while you were gone?

301
00:16:15,480 --> 00:16:18,940
Once I decided I wanted to conjure chains

302
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:20,760
Mostly imagery training

303
00:16:20,760 --> 00:16:23,700
Not only did I feel them with my eyes closed

304
00:16:23,700 --> 00:16:26,620
I drew hundreds, maybe thousands of sketches

305
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:29,460
I looked at chains and even tasted them

306
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:30,920
Smelled and listened

307
00:16:30,920 --> 00:16:34,220
My master told me to play with them constantly

308
00:16:34,220 --> 00:16:36,380
So that's exactly what I did

309
00:16:36,380 --> 00:16:39,740
After a while, he took them away from me

310
00:16:39,740 --> 00:16:42,820
And it was then that I began to hallucinate chains

311
00:16:42,820 --> 00:16:45,620
It wasn't long after that

312
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:47,700
The hallucinations felt heavy

313
00:16:47,700 --> 00:16:50,480
I could feel them, cold and grating

314
00:16:50,480 --> 00:16:52,280
And once that happened

315
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:54,600
I was able to conjure chains myself

316
00:16:54,600 --> 00:16:57,540
But otherwise, it was the same as you

317
00:16:57,540 --> 00:16:58,980
Just Ten and Ren

318
00:16:58,980 --> 00:16:59,900
Kay

319
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:03,140
I've got an idea

320
00:17:03,140 --> 00:17:04,760
You can be my master

321
00:17:04,760 --> 00:17:07,180
You can point out what I'm doing right

322
00:17:07,180 --> 00:17:08,420
And what I've got wrong

323
00:17:08,420 --> 00:17:12,020
This way, I can keep Kura pickup busy

324
00:17:12,020 --> 00:17:13,160
While the auction happens

325
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:15,980
I'm sorry, but I can't

326
00:17:15,980 --> 00:17:16,660
What?

327
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,920
I'm afraid that my boss will be leaving tomorrow

328
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,840
And I'm obligated to accompany her

329
00:17:22,840 --> 00:17:24,720
You're leaving York New?

330
00:17:25,100 --> 00:17:25,600
Yes

331
00:17:25,600 --> 00:17:29,140
Although I'm still concerned about the spiders

332
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:31,340
But it has been two days now

333
00:17:31,340 --> 00:17:34,500
So I suppose they probably left already

334
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:38,120
Well, it's probably for the best

335
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:39,900
But what about you?

336
00:17:40,020 --> 00:17:40,820
Who taught you, Nen?

337
00:17:41,420 --> 00:17:42,560
You should ask them

338
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:44,940
They'd be a better resource than I am

339
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:49,600
A special attack

340
00:17:49,600 --> 00:17:51,300
That's just like you two

341
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,160
I can tell you this much

342
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:56,060
Enhancers really don't need a special attack at all

343
00:17:56,060 --> 00:17:57,120
But why not?

344
00:17:57,960 --> 00:18:00,400
Well, because enhancers are the most balanced

345
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:02,200
Both in offense and defense

346
00:18:02,200 --> 00:18:04,260
If you can master Ten and Ren

347
00:18:04,260 --> 00:18:06,100
You will produce enough force

348
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,900
To be quite destructive indeed

349
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:10,460
What if I don't have that much time?

350
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,920
The screening's just four days away

351
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:13,420
Gon

352
00:18:13,420 --> 00:18:15,560
If I were a judge

353
00:18:15,560 --> 00:18:17,620
I would be very disappointed

354
00:18:17,620 --> 00:18:18,660
If someone showed me

355
00:18:18,660 --> 00:18:20,400
An improvised special attack

356
00:18:20,400 --> 00:18:22,800
Now listen carefully

357
00:18:22,800 --> 00:18:24,700
No matter what happens

358
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:26,960
You must not try to emulate Kurapika

359
00:18:26,960 --> 00:18:29,920
If you think about it

360
00:18:29,920 --> 00:18:32,500
I'm sure you won't need me to tell you why

361
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,340
No, sir

362
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:35,640
So, just be yourself

363
00:18:35,640 --> 00:18:38,160
You're powerful enough on your own merits

364
00:18:38,160 --> 00:18:40,660
That you really have no need to imitate others

365
00:18:40,660 --> 00:18:41,760
You think so?

366
00:18:42,200 --> 00:18:42,780
I do

367
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:46,200
I want you to reflect on each of the things

368
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:47,360
That you're capable of

369
00:18:47,360 --> 00:18:48,740
If you do

370
00:18:48,740 --> 00:18:51,340
You'll find the answer you're looking for

371
00:18:51,340 --> 00:18:55,900
I need a hint

372
00:18:55,900 --> 00:18:56,640
Please

373
00:18:56,640 --> 00:18:58,180
Just a little one

374
00:18:58,180 --> 00:19:00,900
You're starting to sound a little bit desperate

375
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:03,460
Haste makes waste

376
00:19:03,460 --> 00:19:05,680
But hard work always pays off

377
00:19:05,680 --> 00:19:07,260
Yeah, I agree with you

378
00:19:07,260 --> 00:19:09,180
But if it wasn't for this deadline

379
00:19:09,180 --> 00:19:11,700
All right, then here's a hint

380
00:19:11,700 --> 00:19:14,260
When you demonstrated your power

381
00:19:14,260 --> 00:19:15,660
For this Tsesgara person

382
00:19:15,660 --> 00:19:17,860
It was just your normal Ren, right?

383
00:19:18,200 --> 00:19:18,680
Yeah

384
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:22,040
